WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:02.640
SPEAKER 1: BigQuery is
Google's fully managed,

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:06.610
petabyte-scale, low cost
analytics data warehouse.

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:08.790
Let's see how to use
BigQuery with C#.

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:11.770
First, make sure the API
is enabled in your project.

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:14.250
A service account exists
to make API calls,

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:17.220
and proper access control
is set up for BigQuery.

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:19.770
All are explained in the
codelab in the video notes.

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:24.730
In class shell, let's create a
simple .net console app and add

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:27.460
BigQuery API NuGet
package to the project.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:31.660
Open the online code editor
and navigate to program.cs.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:34.030
We will query a sample
table called Shakespeare.

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:36.340
It contains the number of
times each word appears

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:38.320
in each work of Shakespeare.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:40.330
Let's count the total
number of each word.

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:44.110
Reference to BigQuery library,
create a BigQuery client,

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:48.090
and get the table that
we are interested in.

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:53.760
Construct the SQL to count the
words, and execute the query.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:56.080
Finally, print the results.

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:56.970
Let's run the app.

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:57.540
There you go.

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:00.710
You just used BigQuery with C#.

